description:
Motivation and summary: Long-lived paged KV caches can fragment over time when small allocations and frees interleave with variable context lengths. This PR implements a compact block allocator that performs adaptive compaction during low-utilization windows and a time-bounded reuse window for recently freed blocks to improve hot-path cache locality. The goal is to reduce fragmentation, increase block reuse, and improve coalesced GPU memory access for kernel-friendly layouts while keeping eviction stalls under latency SLOs.

What changed (high level): added a CompactBlockAllocator component under runtime/kv_cache that tracks free fragments with age buckets, a compaction worker that consolidates adjacent free fragments when fragmentation_ratio exceeds a dynamic threshold, and an LRU-esque reuse window that preferentially reassigns recently-freed blocks (within a tunable window) to new allocations to increase prefix/KV reuse across continuous-batching windows. The allocator exposes new runtime metrics and a feature flag to gate compaction and pinning heuristics. The implementation coordinates with the continuous batching scheduler to pre-pin predicted hot pages for the next epoch when batch predictors signal affinity.

Key design points: adaptive_compaction_threshold: computed from observed free-fragment-size distribution and eviction pressure; compaction runs only when system token throughput is below a configurable util_percent (default 45%) to avoid impacting p99. Reuse window: age-bucketed FIFO of recently freed blocks with max_age_ticks configurable (default 4). Pinning: per-request pin tokens that keep a block resident across the request lifecycle; pinning is opportunistic — if eviction pressure is high we downgrade pins to soft-pins which are skippable by the eviction path. Kernel layout changes: contiguous mapping for multi-page KV items to enable coalesced loads in the attention kernel; small packing path kept for tiny KV entries to avoid waste.

Files touched (high level): runtime/kv_cache/compact_allocator.rs, runtime/kv_cache/compaction_worker.rs, runtime/kv_cache/metrics.rs, runtime/kv_cache/tests/allocator_tests.rs, runtime/scheduler/batching_integration.rs, runtime/scheduler/prediction.rs, docs/architecture/kv_compaction.md, tools/benchmarks/kv_fragmentation_bench.py, ci/workflows/kv-allocator.yml, examples/allocator_tuning.toml, scripts/rollout_toggle.sh.

Light diff excerpt (illustrative):
--- a/runtime/kv_cache/allocator.rs
+++ b/runtime/kv_cache/compact_allocator.rs
@@ -120,6 +120,24 @@ pub fn allocate(&mut self, size: usize) -> Option<BlockHandle> {
+    // prefer blocks in the reuse window to maximise prefix reuse across batching windows
+    if let Some(handle) = self.reuse_window.find_fit(size) {
+        track_metric!("kv.block_reuse", 1);
+        return Some(handle);
+    }
+
+    // fallback: regular free-list search and occasional compaction trigger
+    if self.fragmentation_ratio() > self.adaptive_threshold() && self.can_compact() {
+        self.compaction_worker.schedule();
+    }
@@
